We are in method public synchronized boolean add(E e). It appends element e to end, returns true. After execution, the last element in the vector (i.e., element at index size()-1) should be null if e is null, else equal to e.

We need to use observer methods: we have get(int index) maybe, or lastElement(), elementAt, etc. Use this.lastElement() maybe. The method is synchronized, but we can call this.lastElement() after addition. Also need size() maybe.

Spec: If e == null then this.lastElement() == null else this.lastElement().equals(e). Since generic type E, need to use equals? For null case, direct equality. For non-null, use equals.

